LAST_SUCCESS=Task 117 M2 step 1 DONE — playback shape added to wandr-video and proven on desktop/VP9. Chunk{data,timestamp_us:i64} -> I420Ref.timestamp_us, plus flush()/reset(). 10/10 crate tests green; host builds. PROVEN: PTS survives the codec unchanged+correctly paired (incl. values that would wrap a 90kHz u32), seek-by-reset resumes at the right frame/PTS without reopening, frames pace against an external clock within one 60Hz tick => A/V sync is expressible.
NOTES=PTS rides through libvpx user_priv (exact; a FIFO would desync since a packet can yield 0 frames). Call path converts 90kHz->us at the video_desktop.rs boundary. ‼️ flush()/reset() are NOT proven and CANNOT be on libvpx: injecting a no-op for each left all tests passing, because a VP9 keyframe already resets references and lag_in_frames=0 means no tail is ever held. Delta-frame probing does not distinguish either (measured: BadFrame either way). They must be validated on MediaCodec (AMediaCodec_flush really discards) in step 2+. Limitation is documented in the tests themselves. NEXT: step 1b = wire the playback path into video_desktop.rs + a --video-playback-test that paces real frames and reports drift; OR step 2 = H.264 (openh264 SW first, then HW).
